        "type": "infoBreak",
        "content": "Topic: Consonant + vowel build. Format: Short paragraph text bubble form."
      },
      {
        "type": "infoBreak",
        "content": "In certain words in Japanese, there is a vowel extension. Ifyou noticed, \"ohayougozaimasu\" is pronounced \"ohayoogozaimasu\", where the end of the \"ohayou\" is stretched out to an \"ohayoo\". Similarly, \"arigatougozaimasu\" is stretched out to \"arigatoogozaimasu\", and \"sayounara\" is stretched out to \"sayoonara\" You will get used to it over time! "
      }
